From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] windows.globalization: ApplicationLanguages

ApplicationLanguages did not exist. React Native for Windows (OneDrive's interface) asks it for the languages to show itself in, and OneDrive stopped with an unhandled exception. Languages is now the user's UI languages, with the program's PrimaryLanguageOverride first; an empty override clears it and a string that is no language tag is refused. ManifestLanguages is the user's languages (a program without a package manifest), and GetLanguagesForUser gives the running user's.
---
diff --git a/dlls/windows.globalization/Makefile.in b/dlls/windows.globalization/Makefile.in
index 83bae11..9d9243f 100644
--- a/dlls/windows.globalization/Makefile.in
+++ b/dlls/windows.globalization/Makefile.in
@@ -2,6 +2,7 @@ MODULE = windows.globalization.dll
 IMPORTS = combase uuid user32
 
 SOURCES = \
+	app_languages.c \
 	classes.idl \
 	geographic_region.c \
 	main.c \
diff --git a/dlls/windows.globalization/app_languages.c b/dlls/windows.globalization/app_languages.c
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..4cd4651
--- /dev/null
+++ b/dlls/windows.globalization/app_languages.c
@@ -0,0 +1,229 @@
+/* WinRT Windows.Globalization.ApplicationLanguages
+ *
+ * Copyright 2026 Stained Glass OS
+ *
